---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import FlowDiagram from '../components/diagrams/FlowDiagram.astro';

const checks = [
  { title: 'Authentic', text: 'Only signals from the system’s own alerts are accepted. Anything else is rejected at the door.' },
  { title: 'Known and switched on', text: 'The signal belongs to a registered strategy, and that strategy is currently enabled. Each strategy can be paused on its own.' },
  { title: 'In the universe', text: 'The coin is on the list of approved markets, and on the strategy’s own list where it has one.' },
  { title: 'Not a duplicate', text: 'A signal that was already handled for the same candle is dropped, so a repeated alert never trades twice.' },
  { title: 'Room for it', text: 'The strategy has a free position slot, or room for another tranche in the position it already holds.' },
  { title: 'No clash', text: 'Where it matters, a coin that the futures strategy already holds is skipped, so two strategies do not pile into the same coin.' },
  { title: 'Enough cash', text: 'There is enough free cash for the order, with a reserve kept aside.' },
  { title: 'Big enough', text: 'The order meets the exchange’s minimum size, so it does not fail halfway.' },
];

const markets = [
  { name: 'ATR Mean Reversion', market: 'Spot', lev: 'None' },
  { name: 'RSI Mean Reversion', market: 'Spot', lev: 'None' },
  { name: 'RSI Red Legs, coins', market: 'Spot', lev: 'None' },
  { name: 'Ichimoku Trend Following', market: 'Spot', lev: 'None' },
  { name: 'RSI Red Legs, QQQ', market: 'Perpetual-style future', lev: 'Leveraged' },
  { name: 'Cross-Sectional Momentum', market: 'Dated futures, isolated margin', lev: '1.5x' },
];
---

<Base title="How it works | Trading B(u)y Signal" description="How a signal becomes a trade: alerts and schedules, the checks in between, execution on OKX Europe and a record of every step.">
  <section class="head dark grain">
    <header class="site-header wrap">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/">Trading B(u)y Signal</a>
      <a class="back" href="/">Back to start page</a>
    </header>
    <div class="wrap intro">
      <h1>How it works</h1>
      <p class="tagline">From a signal to a filled order, without anyone clicking a button. Every step is checked, and every step is written down.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap visual">
      <FlowDiagram />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block grain" aria-labelledby="signals-title">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="kicker">1. Signals</p>
      <h2 id="signals-title">Where trades start</h2>
      <p>Each strategy is a fixed set of rules. Before it trades real money, it is backtested over several years of data and then forward-tested on live prices. New strategies first run in a test mode, in which the system records what it would do without placing any orders.</p>
      <div class="pair">
        <div>
          <h3>Alerts from TradingView</h3>
          <p>Four strategies run as scripts on TradingView. When their rules are met, they send an alert with the strategy, the coin and the action. Some react at the close of a daily or 4-hour candle; others have orders waiting at a price level, which can fill at any time of day.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>A weekly schedule</h3>
          <p>Cross-Sectional Momentum does not wait for alerts. Once a week, a scheduled job fetches fresh prices from an independent data source, ranks the coins and rebalances the positions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block dark grain" aria-labelledby="bridge-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">2. The bridge</p>
      <h2 id="bridge-title">Every signal is checked</h2>
      <p class="lead">Alerts go to a small server, the bridge, which sits between TradingView and the exchange. Before it acts on a buy signal, all of these checks have to pass:</p>
      <ul class="checks" data-checks>
        {checks.map((c, i) => (
          <li style={`--i:${i}`}>
            <span class="lamp" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <h3>{c.title}</h3>
            <p>{c.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="verdict" style={`--i:${checks.length}`}>
        <span class="lamp" aria-hidden="true"></span>All clear: the order goes out.
      </p>
      <div class="notes">
        <p class="note">If a check fails, the signal is logged and skipped. Nothing is forced through, and a refused signal can be retried safely.</p>
        <p class="note">After a market-wide sell-off, many alerts can arrive within seconds. Each strategy’s signals are handled one at a time, and a slot is reserved before any order is placed, so the limits hold even then.</p>
        <p class="note">The weekly job for Cross-Sectional Momentum runs its own checks: it only trades when the price data for every coin is complete and up to date, and it confirms that last week’s positions are closed before it opens new ones.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block grain" aria-labelledby="exec-title">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="kicker">3. Execution</p>
      <h2 id="exec-title">Orders on OKX Europe</h2>
      <p>All trades run on OKX Europe, the exchange’s EU platform. Spot trades are made against USDC. Each strategy has its own budget and its own book of positions.</p>
      <table class="markets">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Strategy</th><th scope="col">Market</th><th scope="col">Leverage</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {markets.map((m) => (
            <tr><th scope="row">{m.name}</th><td>{m.market}</td><td>{m.lev}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>Orders are placed at market. Large orders are split into smaller pieces to keep the price impact low.</li>
        <li>Every fill is confirmed with the exchange before the position is recorded, using the amount actually filled.</li>
        <li>When two strategies hold the same coin, each one tracks only its own share, and a sell signal only ever sells what that strategy bought.</li>
        <li>The futures positions use isolated margin, so a loss in one position can never draw on the rest of the account.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block dark grain" aria-labelledby="records-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">4. Records and control</p>
      <h2 id="records-title">Every step is written down</h2>
      <div class="grid4">
        <div>
          <h3>Logs</h3>
          <p>Every signal, every decision, every order and every fill is logged with its time, including the signals that were refused.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Saved state</h3>
          <p>Each strategy’s open positions are saved after every change, so a restart picks up exactly where it stopped.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Reconciliation</h3>
          <p>The recorded positions are regularly checked against the exchange by hand. Differences are investigated, not ignored.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Trade tracker</h3>
          <p>Closed trades are collected per strategy, with entry, exit, size and result, so every strategy can be judged on its own.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Head ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  .head {
    padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
  }
  .site-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-block: 1.75rem clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.5rem);
  }
  .wordmark {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .back {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--on-dark-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .back:hover {
    color: var(--gold-bright);
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.75rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: #f2f1ee;
  }
  .tagline {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    max-width: 36rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.8vw, 1.25rem);
    color: var(--on-dark-muted);
  }
  .visual {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  /* Blocks ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
  .block {
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 6.5rem);
  }
  .narrow > * {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }
  .kicker {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem !important;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--gold) !important;
  }
  .block:not(.dark) .kicker {
    color: #8a6d33 !important;
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  .dark h2 {
    color: #f2f1ee;
  }
  .block p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .dark p {
    color: var(--on-dark-muted);
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }
  .dark h3 {
    color: #f2f1ee;
  }
  .pair {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.75rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .pair > div,
  .grid4 > div {
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .grid4 > div {
    border-top-color: var(--rule);
  }
  .pair p,
  .grid4 p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .plain {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .plain li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  /* Checks ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
  .lead {
    max-width: 40rem;
  }
  .checks {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .checks li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.5rem 3.25rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .checks p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .lamp {
    position: absolute;
    left: 1.5rem;
    top: 1.85rem;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1px solid var(--on-dark-muted);
    transition:
      background-color 300ms ease calc(var(--i) * 180ms),
      border-color 300ms ease calc(var(--i) * 180ms),
      box-shadow 300ms ease calc(var(--i) * 180ms);
  }
  [data-checks].lit .lamp,
  .lit ~ .verdict .lamp {
    background: var(--gold-bright);
    border-color: var(--gold-bright);
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px 2px rgba(230, 201, 136, 0.55);
  }
  .verdict {
    position: relative;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0 !important;
    padding-left: 1.75rem;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.4vw, 1.625rem);
    color: var(--on-dark-muted) !important;
    transition: color 400ms ease calc(var(--i) * 180ms);
  }
  .verdict .lamp {
    left: 0;
    top: 0.55em;
  }
  .lit ~ .verdict {
    color: var(--gold-bright) !important;
  }
  .notes {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .note {
    max-width: 44rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--gold);
    margin: 0 !important;
  }

  /* Markets table --------------------------------------------------------- */
  .markets {
    width: 100%;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .markets th,
  .markets td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.65rem 1rem 0.65rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .markets thead th {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--muted);
    border-bottom-color: var(--ink);
  }
  .markets tbody th {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .markets td {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  /* Records --------------------------------------------------------------- */
  .grid4 {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 60rem) {
    .checks,
    .grid4 {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .checks,
    .grid4 {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .markets th,
    .markets td {
      padding-right: 0.6rem;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  const list = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-checks]');
  if (list) {
    const io = new IntersectionObserver(
      ([e]) => {
        if (e.isIntersecting) {
          list.classList.add('lit');
          io.disconnect();
        }
      },
      { threshold: 0.4 },
    );
    io.observe(list);
  }
</script>
